{lo broda pu brode} is parsed differently between jbofi'e (yacc) and camxes=
=20
(peg):

jbofi'e
[(lo broda KU) CU <<pu brode>> VAU]

camxes
[(lo broda KU) (pu KU) CU <<brode>> VAU]

It seems that jbofi'e is in accordance with CLL, while camxes isn't.
(cf.
CLL9.10:
An alternative to using =93ku=94 is to place the modal cmavo right before t=
he=20
selbri, following the =93cu=94 which often appears there. When a modal is=
=20
present, the =93cu=94 is almost never necessary.
CLL10.1:
The placement of a tense construct within a Lojban bridi is easy: right=20
before the selbri. It goes immediately after the =93cu=94, and can in fact=
=20
always replace the =93cu=94 (although in very complex sentences the rules f=
or=20
eliding terminators may be changed as a result).
)


